                 methodological review, meta-epidemiological review and research
                 on research. Methodological studies have previously been used
                 to examine the characteristics of certain tools or methods used
                 in research, to examine the adherence of reporting guidelines
                 by researchers, to advance the methodology of certain methods,
                 to examine the heterogeneity and exploring causes of research
                 methodologies and to develop new methodologies. Recent findings
                 To date, the guidance to undertake methodological studies is
                 limited. Some studies used either systematic, scoping or
                 mapping approach to undertake them. This narrative review will
                 present a summary of published methodological studies guidance
