  number    =  4,
  pages     = "950--952",
  abstract  = "ABSTRACT: Evidence synthesis encompasses a broad range of review
               types, and scoping reviews are an increasingly popular approach
               to synthesizing evidence in a number of fields. They sit
               alongside other evidence synthesis methodologies, such as
               systematic reviews, qualitative evidence synthesis, realist
               synthesis, and many more. Until now, scoping reviews have been
               variously defined in the literature. In this article, we provide
